/*
Problem: Maximum Average Subarray I (LC 643)
Topic: Sliding Window

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

The subarray size is fixed (k).

Instead of computing the sum of every
subarray from scratch, maintain a
sliding window of size k.

As the window moves:

• Add the new element.

• Remove the outgoing element.

• Update the maximum average.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Initialize:

   left = 0

   sum = 0

2. Traverse the array.

3. Add the current element to the
   window sum.

4. Once the window size becomes k:

   • Compute the average.

   • Update the maximum average.

   • Remove the leftmost element.

   • Move the left pointer.

5. Return the maximum average.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

nums = [1,12,-5,-6,50,3]

k = 4

Windows:

[1,12,-5,-6]

Average = 0.5

[12,-5,-6,50]

Average = 12.75

[-5,-6,50,3]

Average = 10.5

Answer:

12.75

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

The window size always remains k.

Instead of recomputing each window's
sum, we reuse the previous sum by
adding one element and removing one
element.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Each element enters and leaves the
window exactly once.

Space : O(1)

Only a few variables are used.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Sliding Window (Fixed Size)
*/

class Solution {
public:
    double findMaxAverage(vector<int>& nums, int k) {

        int left = 0;

        double sum = 0;
        double maxAvg = INT_MIN;

        for (int right = 0;
             right < nums.size();
             right++) {

            // Expand window
            sum += nums[right];

            // Wait until window size becomes k
            if (right - left + 1 < k)
                continue;

            // Compute current average
            double avg = sum / k;

            maxAvg = max(maxAvg, avg);

            // Slide window
            sum -= nums[left];
            left++;
        }

        return maxAvg;
    }
};
